+# Mobile-first Autopilot shortcuts
+
+The mobile interface avoids long quoted prompts and manual mission commands.
+
+## Inspect one file
+
+```bash
+hai csuf-email.md
+```
+
+Add a short question without quotation marks:
+
+```bash
+hai csuf-email.md what do I do next
+```
+
+`hai` reads the current file, including an untracked or locally modified copy,
+runs independent verification, prints the answer, and archives it under
+`~/.hermes/autopilot/answers/`.
+
+## Make a change
+
+```bash
+ham create NOTES.md from README.md
+```
+
+Quotation marks are optional. Dirty repositories are handled through an
+isolated shadow and verified changes are applied only when they do not overlap
+existing local edits.
+
+## Paste long text
+
+```bash
+hapaste
+```
+
+Paste the content and finish with a line containing only `.done`. The pasted
+text is stored only in a temporary local scratch file, analyzed in an isolated
+mission, and removed after completion. Piped standard input is also supported:
+
+```bash
+cat message.txt | hapaste
+```
+
+## Safety behavior
+
+- Dates and web addresses in pasted prose are not treated as repository paths.
+- Missing source files fail before mission creation and include a close-name
+  suggestion when available.
+- Vague tasks such as `test` are rejected before spending model time.
+- Commands refuse to start from Hermes shadow and mission-worktree folders.
